  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "The initial velocity of a particle is $(5i-j)\\,\\text{km/h}.$ Find the speed of the particle after $2$ hours if the particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(i+3j)\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nu=5i-j,\\,a=i+3j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $2$ hours, the velocity of the particle will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\  & =(5i-j)+(i+3j)(2) \\\\  & =(5i-j)+(2i+6j) \\\\  & =(7i+5j)\\,\\text{km/h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the speed of the particle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v| & =|7i+5j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{7}^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{74}\\,\\text{km/h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
